			},
			"date": "2025-01-28T02:24:39.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> This is most Chinese websites. If you are already on the phone they just redirect you to the appstore; there is no remote installing app through the web (like Google Play). Everyone pays offline through QR-code based apps. It is quite a hassle to find a non-searchbar and type some English in. As long as you put a QR code up people know to take out the phone, which gets more used than whatever this got scanned from. Just unfortunate that shortlink isn’t a priority.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
